ideas.algorithm:
a=x (vector); amp=1; f=F0.
for k in 0..K-1:
  a=Rot*a (fixed orthonormal matrix per dimension, 3-4-5 rotation in 2D)
  for each axis j: s_j=sin(f*a_j+phase(seed,k,j))
  for each axis j: a_j+=Couple*amp*s_(j+1 mod d)
  sum+=amp*product_j(s_j); nrm+=amp; amp*=Gain; f*=Lac (irrational, ~1.47)
Output sum/nrm*scale, clamp.
Couple is Gardner's phase shifting taken to feedback. Couple=0 gives a plain Gardner sum.
